description:
Zafirov v. Florida Medical Associates, which had held that the qui tam provisions violate the Appointments Clause of Article II.
The government declined to intervene, but she continued to pursue the litigation on behalf of the United States as a relator.
), where arguments raised on appeal include whether the qui tam provisions violate the Appointments, Vesting, and Take Care Clauses of Article II.
), where two judges have expressed skepticism of the qui tam provisions’ constitutionality.
But, as noted, its decision is a narrow one, and it leaves significant constitutional issues unresolved and several avenues for defendants facing qui tam litigation to continue to pursue.
